From: Jim Huang <jserv@ccns.ncku.edu.tw>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: expose uncompressed kernel image mode

The current boot flow consumes arch/arm/boot/Image directly through the
bootwrapper rather than the zImage self-decompressor. Future XIP work has
the same requirement: kernel text must remain plaintext.

ARM already wires the compressed image choices in init/Kconfig, but it does
not select HAVE_KERNEL_UNCOMPRESSED, so CONFIG_KERNEL_UNCOMPRESSED is never
offered and olddefconfig falls back to CONFIG_KERNEL_GZIP=y.

Expose the uncompressed choice on ARM so build.sh can pin
CONFIG_KERNEL_UNCOMPRESSED=y and keep the kernel image mode aligned with the
actual boot path.

diff -urN a/arch/arm/Kconfig b/arch/arm/Kconfig
--- a/arch/arm/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/Kconfig
@@ -117,6 +117,7 @@
 	select HAVE_KERNEL_GZIP
 	select HAVE_KERNEL_LZ4
 	select HAVE_KERNEL_LZMA
+	select HAVE_KERNEL_UNCOMPRESSED
 	select HAVE_KERNEL_LZO
 	select HAVE_KERNEL_XZ
 	select HAVE_KPROBES if !XIP_KERNEL && !CPU_ENDIAN_BE32 && !CPU_V7M
